cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use Cppuccino in teaching or research, please cite it as below."
title: "Cppuccino: a bilingual C++ notebook with runnable proof"
abstract: >-
  Cppuccino is a bilingual English/Chinese C++ learning repository. It pairs
  concept articles with failure-mode articles, runnable examples, staged
  projects, and an interactive arcade whose boss fights reproduce real
  sanitizer failures.
authors:
  - family-names: "polarours"
repository-code: "https://github.com/polarours/Cppuccino"
url: "https://polarours.github.io/Cppuccino/"
license: MIT
version: "1.0.0"
date-released: "2026-11-26"
keywords:
  - C++
  - C++20
  - C++23
  - undefined behavior
  - sanitizers
  - bilingual education
  - computer science education
type: software
